Drive the audio device on the network thread, and cameras on a thread of their own

WebRTC M158 has no worker thread apart from the network thread: the worker thread of
PeerConnectionFactoryDependencies and the CreatePeerConnectionFactory overload that took
one are gone, and the voice engine, with the audio device module it drives, runs where
ICE, DTLS and RTP do. The factory made a worker thread of its own, handed it to WebRTC,
and made and drove the audio device module there. It now does all of that on the network
thread, the one thread the voice engine calls the module on: the module is used from one
thread only, and on Linux it connects again there to a sound server that went away
(WebRTC patch 0006), which needs it made there. The audio device's lists, its choice of
devices and its volumes (patch 0010) are done there as before, by a blocking call or a
task from the caller's thread; the audio processing and the custom audio transport are
made there. Cameras (VcmCapturer), which nothing of WebRTC calls and which may take a
while to open, start and stop, are opened, started and stopped on a thread of their own,
capture_thread, in place of the worker thread.

